 ## The Process
 
+### 0. Closeout Gate (Unresolved Findings)
+
+**Deterministic enforcement of the Iron Law.** Before any other check, refuse
+completion if deep review left unresolved Critical or Important findings. This is
+a script with an exit code, not a prompt, so it holds even in autonomous mode
+where prompt-level "DO NOT proceed" guidance can be skipped.
+
+```bash
+CLOSEOUT_GATE="$(find ~/.claude -name 'spex-closeout-gate.sh' 2>/dev/null | head -1)"
+if [ -x "$CLOSEOUT_GATE" ]; then
+  "$CLOSEOUT_GATE" || exit 1
+fi
+```
+
+**If the gate exits non-zero:**
+- STOP. Do not run the remaining steps. Do not claim completion.
+- Report the unresolved Critical/Important findings from
+  `specs/<feature>/review-findings.md`, then resolve them or re-run
+  `speckit.spex-deep-review.run` before retrying verification.
+
+**If no `review-findings.md` exists** (deep review not run), the gate passes and
+verification continues normally. Set `SPEX_CLOSEOUT_STRICT=1` to require a
+parseable, clean findings file before completion.
+
 ### 1. Run Tests
 
 **Execute all tests:**
